{
 "_doc": "The default personality set (2026-11-08, the author's sets decision): idle actions (from idle.json: Idle actions of the desktop companion (2026-11-04, spec in CLAUDE.md): small things the avatar does every 20-60 s while nobody talks to it. Model-free keyframes (the perform format); 'sit' actions are solved for whichever floor posture the avatar is in. Each starts and ends in the posture's rest pose. Written by Claude, no dataset. hands_behind (palms together behind the back) removed 2026-11-05 (the author: odd as an idle action).) and touch reactions (from touch.json: Touch reactions (2026-11-06, grilling with the author Q5-Q7): clicking a body part in the companion window plays one of these, solved for the model and posture like idle.json (companion /touch?posture=&turn=). 'stand' is used when standing, 'sit' for every floor posture. Each has the emotion the face shows. Sided ones (_r / _l) are the character's own right / left. shy_cover answers the chest, shy_skirt the skirt / front of the hips, shy_bottom the bottom (sitting: shy_skirt). Versions of one reaction are named <name>~2, <name>~3 and play in turn on repeated clicks (the author, 2026-11-08: no escalation, no angry face from repeated clicks). A reaction that fails the rule filter for a model / posture is dropped at solve time; the page then falls back along TOUCH_FALLBACK.). Format: sets/<name>.json = {title: {zh, en, ja}, idle: {stand: [...], sit: [...]}, touch: {stand: [...], sit: [...]}}; an entry is {name, emotion, keyframes[, interp]} or {name, use: '<name>' | '<set>:<name>'} (the same motion under another item's name, e.g. shy shoulder = chest). The companion (companion.mjs /idle, /touch ?set=) solves a set's entries per model / posture / facing; the page falls back to this set for an item the chosen set lacks (or the filter dropped), and <name>~2 / ~3 are versions played in turn.",
